        "q8": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is virtual staging legal in Texas?",
            "answer": "Yes. Virtual staging is a standard marketing practice; the rule is not to misrepresent the property. Add furniture and decor only, don't hide defects or change permanent features, and disclose that photos are virtually staged — the NAR Code of Ethics expects it. Check NTREIS rules for exact labeling; every Bella order includes disclosure guidance."
          }
